WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's very nice. Thank you

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:06.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
Someone said to me,
"You look young from far away.

00:00:06.373 --> 00:00:08.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Light laughter ]
And I think it might be

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:11.077 size:75% position:38%
the worst compliment
I've ever heard...

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
...in my life.

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:15.615
It has a real M. Night Shyamalan
twist at the end,

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:16.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
doesn't it?
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You look young."
"Yeah?"

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:19.319 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"From far away."

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Wow!
I did not see that coming.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:22.355 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:25.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
You are mean from up close
is what you are.

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:26.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I...

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't like you
from this distance.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:31.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm trying to stay young,
you know, and move.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:31.831 size:78% position:39% line:92%
We don't move enough.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:35.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
Isn't that a weird
modern-day health concern?

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:35.668 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But it's true.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:38.772
Do you ever sit sedentary
for 36 hours and just go,

00:00:38.772 --> 00:00:41.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Boy, I don't feel well
right now."

00:00:41.241 --> 00:00:41.808 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:44.110
I think
it's going to baffle historians.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.311 line:92%
"What happened to these people?"

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:48.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
"They just stopped.
We're not sure."

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:48.581 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:51.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
"They kind of slowly coalesced
into a gel,

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.453 line:92%
and that was it for them.

00:00:53.453 --> 00:00:54.187 size:78% position:39% line:92%
We have evidence that

00:00:54.187 --> 00:00:57.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
they were actually countin
their individual steps

00:00:57.924 --> 00:01:00.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
one at a time."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
"That's how little
they were moving."

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:05.432 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.135 line:92%
My friends are into running.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:12.072
And they say stuff like,
"I'm addicted to running,"

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I cannot
wrap my head around.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:17.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
I am so addicted
to stopping running.

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:19.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I can't stop stopping running.

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
The whole time I'm running
all I'm thinking is,

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:23.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
"When does the addiction
kick in?"

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:24.350 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
Most things that are addictive
take action quick,

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
but this running seems to be
a bit of an outlier --

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
can we agree?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:32.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, you see people run
who are meant to run.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
They look graceful
and efficient.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.694 line:92%
The whole time I'm running

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.930
there's this thought going
over and over in my head,

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is,
"I've never seen me run,

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:40.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I don't think
this looks right."

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.501 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:41.501 --> 00:01:44.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
"One leg is doing far more wor
than it should.

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:47.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
I might be skipping right now.
I'm not certain."

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:50.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So...

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:52.112 size:81% position:41% line:92%
[ Laughter continues ]

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:54.013 line:92%
Little things are happening.

00:01:54.013 --> 00:01:55.915 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I fell down.

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.250 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I used to trip.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:58.651 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.153 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Do you understand?

00:02:00.153 --> 00:02:01.221 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:02.789 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Here's how life goes.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.491 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Tripping -- young.

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:06.826 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Falling -- old.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.628 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:11.197 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I fell down.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.365 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was significant.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:13.766 line:92%
I'm calling it an adult fall

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:17.003 size:81% position:41%
And I say that because
I remember as a child

00:02:17.003 --> 00:02:19.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
adults talking to other adults
about falling

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:21.207 line:92%
in very hushed, serious tones.

00:02:21.207 --> 00:02:23.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you remember
those conversations?

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.644 size:78% position:39% line:92%
"Ryan, Grandma fell."

00:02:24.644 --> 00:02:27.614 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:29.282 line:92%
"Did you tell her to get up?

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:30.817 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:33.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I fell six times.
It's not even noon.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:34.787 line:92%
What do you want from me?"

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:35.555 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I understand now.
I have a little empathy.

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.092 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I had my own adult fall.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:41.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
I fell on the streets
of New York City.

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:43.796
People were around.
I mean, there was no denying it.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.665 line:92%
Everyone asked, "Are you okay?

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:48.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes, but let me make
this point --

00:02:48.168 --> 00:02:49.202 size:81% position:41% line:92%
not everyone meant it.

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:51.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's true.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
Two 25-year-old girls
on the street go,

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
"[Chuckles] Are you okay?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.709 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I mean, there was...

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:57.877 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.679 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:00.847 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Chuckles ]

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:02.048 size:81% position:41% line:92%
[ Applause continues ]

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
...zero empathy
in their reaction.

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:05.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
The words
came out of their mouths.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
What they
actually communicated was,

00:03:07.253 --> 00:03:08.655 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I wish my camera was on
for that.

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was spectacular."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.258 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Are you okay?"

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:16.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
Has anyone ever answered, "No,
to, "Are you okay?"

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.464 line:92%
in the history of falling down

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:21.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
My body was screaming
I was not okay,

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:24.304 line:92%
and I still said, "I'm fine.

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:25.104 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:27.440 line:92%
"I want to die alone right here.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:32.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
Put the orange cones around me
and leave me alone."

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.280 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:39.619 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:40.286 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Are you okay?"

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:43.156
What am I supposed to say to two
25-year-old girls on the street?

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:46.559
"No, can you two petite children
take me to the hospital"?

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:47.126 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:50.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
"What are you gonna do?
Go get a grown-up, quick."

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:53.132 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:57.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was with a girl when I fell.
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let me just tell you
the whole story.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:00.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, there we are.
We're at dinner.

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:02.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're enjoying
each other's company.

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:04.777 size:78% position:39%
Over time, I thought
maybe we should date.

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:06.412 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So I brought it up.

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:07.614 line:92%
I said, "Maybe we should date.

00:04:07.614 --> 00:04:11.251
She very kindly,
as gingerly as humanly possible,

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:13.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
said,
"Maybe we should not date.

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Now, it's okay.

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:18.157 size:88% position:44%
I'm -- I'm happy to have
an honest conversation.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:22.528
but then we left the restaurant,
and then I fell down.

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:25.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
And...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:26.633 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Now...

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:30.703 size:81% position:41% line:92%
[ Laughter continues ]

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:32.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
My only wish
for this whole scenario

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:35.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that there could have bee
a little space

00:04:35.141 --> 00:04:36.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
between these two moments.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:38.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's all.
Just, does nobody have my back

00:04:38.444 --> 00:04:42.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is there not one guardian ange
petitioning for me, going,

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:44.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Look, he threw
a curve ball at dinner.

00:04:44.951 --> 00:04:46.352 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Nobody saw that coming.

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:47.620 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Is there any way that

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:51.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
we can push his adult fall
by just a day?"

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:52.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
And...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:55.795
...I can just hear God going
"You know, I would love to

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.363 line:92%
but we've pushed this adult fall

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:58.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
as far as
we can possibly push it."

00:04:58.898 --> 00:05:01.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter and applause ]
"I'm very sorry.

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.302 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Everyone's in place.

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:04.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's simply nothing
I can do."

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:05.905 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:07.206 line:92%
"Anyway, he's gonna be fine.

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.841 line:92%
He looks young from up here.

00:05:08.841 --> 00:05:10.043 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.043 --> 00:05:10.877 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:13.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm Ryan Hamilton.
Thank you very much.

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:14.914 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank you.

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:17.050 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:19.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What? Oh, my God.
What a great set.

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:20.520 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Ryan Hamilton!

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a nice standing ovation
for you there, buddy.

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:25.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well done.
Ryan Hamilton.

